    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea93279f_8668e864",
        "filename": "fs/incfs/stats.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-21T11:51:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why do these all have to be atomic?  What is so important that they hurt the sync of the cpus just for a statistic?  What would ever \"tear\" that really matters here?\n\nWhy can\u0027t you just use a simple u32 and u64 everywhere?  Those should be \"atomic enough\" for unimportant stuff like this and the benefit is that you will not ever slow anything down.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "91eac08cfe7d6ec1fd225b68609aa1534abe4292",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b54226ee_119bebca",
        "filename": "fs/incfs/stats.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1724998
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-21T16:53:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, atomics was used only for correctness; but if this is viewed as informational, yes, we can just use simple u32/u64. \n\nI guess per-cpu counters may help here..",
      "parentUuid": "ea93279f_8668e864",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "91eac08cfe7d6ec1fd225b68609aa1534abe4292",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6081b101_0ae03322",
        "filename": "fs/incfs/stats.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-21T16:59:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t optimize things that you do not even know if they are a problem 😊\nWorry about per-cpu counters only if that\u0027s really needed, just try a single variable first and see how that goes.",
      "parentUuid": "b54226ee_119bebca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "91eac08cfe7d6ec1fd225b68609aa1534abe4292",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c2b85c5_d5e5fe39",
        "filename": "fs/incfs/stats.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1724998
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-21T17:11:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From my past experience, atomics do have overhead (at least on a big system where there are like 96 CPU cores) especially in the hot IO path and more specifically for smaller block size IO (\u003c\u003d 4k). \n\nYes, certainly using single variable helps and probably after some perf runs, we can think of optimization if required.",
      "parentUuid": "6081b101_0ae03322",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "91eac08cfe7d6ec1fd225b68609aa1534abe4292",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dedfb290_63cb45f1",
        "filename": "fs/incfs/stats.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1724998
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T06:26:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All monotonically increasing counters have been moved to to u32/u64.\n\nActive counters need atomics else they will wrap around and will be misleading.",
      "parentUuid": "3c2b85c5_d5e5fe39",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "91eac08cfe7d6ec1fd225b68609aa1534abe4292",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b2fcffc_3711041b",
        "filename": "fs/incfs/stats.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-21T11:51:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why these pointless wrappers?  Just call atomic_inc() as you are forcing us to think of new apis every time we see this (_d for decrement???)\n\nI can understand if you really really want to optimize these away if this isn\u0027t enabled, but see my previous comment about how you probably always want these anyway.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "91eac08cfe7d6ec1fd225b68609aa1534abe4292",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac150969_26c45575",
        "filename": "fs/incfs/stats.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1724998
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-21T16:53:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed. Wrappers were added when CONFIG_INCFS_STATS is not enabled; but if we have stats always, we can remove these wrappers.",
